WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.960
This is bourzik.com — a laboratory of small, smart tools, built with AI.

2
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:16.503
Bourzik Laboratory is a workshop for web tools that explore language, script, data and physics.

3
00:00:16.553 --> 00:00:21.161
Each tool does one thing well, runs entirely in your browser,

4
00:00:21.211 --> 00:00:25.410
and keeps your data on your own device. Free, and open.

5
00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:33.779
Tifinagh Converter writes Amazigh in Arabic or Latin letters and turns it into Tifinagh —

6
00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:35.000
or back again.

7
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:41.454
It converts instantly as you type, follows the official standard alphabet,

8
00:00:41.504 --> 00:00:46.127
and works in three interface languages, even offline.

9
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.834
Genus answers the question every learner of German asks: which article —

10
00:00:52.884 --> 00:00:54.270
der, die, or das?

11
00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:02.974
Look up the gender of nearly 55,000 German nouns, plus Spanish, Italian, French, Portuguese and Dutch —

12
00:01:03.024 --> 00:01:07.840
then drill the ones you keep getting wrong on flip cards.

13
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.925
Bormap maps ideas, people or data as a connected graph —

14
00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:17.930
so you can follow the branches and see how everything relates.

15
00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:22.864
Fruit Jelly Knife is a soft-body physics study.

16
00:01:22.914 --> 00:01:30.327
Pull, wobble and slice a translucent gummy fruit, rendered in real time with WebGPU.

17
00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.871
VECTORSPEC Engine Lab runs four heat engines —

18
00:01:34.921 --> 00:01:40.421
a single piston, a turbo four, a turbofan and a ship's steam plant —

19
00:01:40.471 --> 00:01:45.287
and lets you watch their cycles, limits and failures, live.

20
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:54.514
And CCDV-F Prep Hub helps developers prepare for the Claude Certified Developer – Foundations exam,

21
00:01:54.564 --> 00:01:59.027
with a study guide, flashcards and timed mock exams.

22
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.380
Agent Map puts more than a hundred AI agent tools on one living map.

23
00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.250
Watch them sort themselves by what they do,

24
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.210
build your own stack, and take it with you as JSON.

25
00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:23.387
Seven very different tools: linguistics, data, visualization, real-time physics, engineering simulation, learning, and AI tooling.

26
00:02:24.546 --> 00:02:27.004
That's the range we offer —

27
00:02:27.054 --> 00:02:32.997
from an idea to a working, privacy-first product, powered by AI.

28
00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:38.455
And one more thing. This video was made entirely with AI.

29
00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:44.930
The script, the motion design, the images, the voice you're hearing, the music,

30
00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:50.554
and every sound effect — all generated by AI, and assembled in code.

31
00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:57.050
bourzik.com. Small tools, big ideas. Let's build yours.
